From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] amvecm: cm2: bound color index against the selected color table

The AMVECM_IOC_S_CMS_LUMA / _SAT / _HUE / _HUE_HS handlers take the colour
index from cm_9_color_md or cm_14_color_md depending on color_type, but bound
both with "cm_color <= cm_14_ecm2colormode_max - 1". With the 9-colour table an
index of 9..13 passes and cm2_luma()/sat()/hue()/hue_by_hs() hand it to
color_adj() with the nine-entry color_key_pts[], reading up to five entries past
the array into the adjacent color_start[]/color_end[] statics. The four cm2
debug sysfs stores are worse: color_mode comes from kstrtoul() unbounded and is
used directly as cm2_*_array[color_mode][0] = val, a write past a
[cm_14_ecm2colormode_max][3] array (root only, as CoreELEC runs).

Record the limit matching the selected table and compare against it in the
ioctl handlers; reject an out-of-range colour mode in the sysfs stores via the
existing kfree_buf path. color_adj() itself is unchanged. Not exercised on
hardware.

